      "created_at": "2025-08-31T21:59:41.590Z",
      "cooked": "<p>HI <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/frappe795\">@Frappe795</a>:</p>\n<p>Basically, you should “listen” to field changes and then populate df options on your next select field. But maybe it would more interesting using here Autocomplete field. It’s pretty undocumented, but look at this …</p>\n<div class=\"youtube-onebox lazy-video-container\" data-video-id=\"7xVz4zZiWQs\" data-video-title=\"Working with Autocomplete Field in Frappe Framework\" data-video-start-time=\"\" data-provider-name=\"youtube\">\n  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7xVz4zZiWQs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"video-thumbnail\" rel=\"noopener\">\n    <img class=\"youtube-thumbnail\" src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7xVz4zZiWQs/maxresdefault.jpg\" title=\"Working with Autocomplete Field in Frappe Framework\" width=\"690\" height=\"388\">\n  </a>\n</div>\n\n<p>Hope this helps.</p>",
